From: schoeremy <jeremyfroeb2007@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:19:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 46/55] nxhost nvn: count SAMPLES_PASSED for real with Metal
 visibility results

Every SAMPLES_PASSED report used to read "one more than the last", which
kept occlusion-culled objects visible. Splatoon 3 also measures ink this
way: its paint checker resets the counter, draws a probe that only passes
where there is ink and reads the report (13 resets+reports per frame
already in the menus). One sample per probe meant almost no ink, so
swimming never sped up and inked walls could not be climbed.

Draws after a reset now count into slots of a shared visibility buffer
(one per counter interval and render pass, Accumulate mode, zeroed when
handed out); a report sums its interval's slots once the command buffer
has completed (completion handler, nvnSyncWait, next submit) and writes
the value with the timestamp. Intervals with draws that could not be
encoded fall back to the old fake value when they counted nothing.
NX_REAL_OCCLUSION=0 restores the fake counter; NX_TRACE_OCCLUSION=1 logs
the resolved reports. Menus render completely with real counts.

